+## Current checkpoint — Phase 13C, 2026-10-01
+
+**Phase 13A and 13B ACCEPTED / CLOSED. Phase 13C IMPLEMENTED / READY FOR FINAL REVIEW.
+Phase 13 IN PROGRESS; Phase 14 NOT STARTED.** Brian explicitly approves
+[the privacy policy](../IMAGE_PRIVACY_POLICY.md), terminology correction,
+0017 production migration/deployment, private Linux storage and combined recovery.
+Accepted 13B local commit: `1c7501092e7fad92a5471fa5571c6d009a1b0c3f`,
+`Implement Phase 13B marketplace intake UI`; exact eleven-file closeout reused
+accepted checks without test/browser/build reruns. Main remains unpushed.
+
+The authorized sequence is focused backup-format/capture seam validation, one
+wording check and immutable release build, fresh production admission, one verified
+pre-migration dual backup and supported proof, guarded 0017 migration/grants,
+release/storage activation, one retained synthetic intake, one combined dual backup,
+then independent Windows Drive-only off-host restore of that same recovery set.
+Historical receipts/pins remain unchanged. No live retention deletion, Android build,
+provider work or later phase is included. On ambiguous live failure stop mutations,
+inspect durable evidence and preserve user data; never automatically downgrade/drop
+new tables or restore over newer activity. Details: [recovery runbook](../IMAGE_BACKUP_RECOVERY.md).
+
+- [x] Accepted 13B closeout, empty index and protected hashes.
+- [x] Fresh admission: expected release/0016, generation 1, 28,278 sets,
+  normal health, no failed units or maintenance conflicts; data disk has ample space.
+- [x] Eight focused seams, affected static checks, one wording case and one final normal immutable release.
+- [x] Guarded 0017 migration/grants, release/private storage and one retained three-image synthetic intake.
+- [x] One normal combined dual capture; same-set independent Drive-only off-host restore and cleanup.
+- [x] Fourteen final normal health checks, active services/timers, zero failed units and sanitized r1 review package.
+
+### Phase 13C completed evidence
+
+Production is `phase13c-marketplace-intake-r1`, `0017_listing_images`; catalog
+remains generation 1, one accepted nonsynthetic snapshot and 28,278 sets.
+One harmless synthetic intake retains three originals, thumbnails and durable
+receipts in positions 0–2, next_display_order 3. Peak uploads were two. Authenticated
+original bytes matched, refresh/reopen passed, private responses were no-store,
+no private service-worker entries appeared, sign-out revoked nine object URLs,
+and one logged-out image request returned 401. Manual/unknown-source images and
+thumbnails retain the stricter restricted classification. No Delete was invented.
+
+The single post-intake normal backup service completed in 376 seconds. It paused
+the API/health timers through capture/readback, exported one read-only database
+snapshot, and streamed four artifacts to both encrypted destinations. All eight
+readbacks, bytes/hashes and repository checks passed. Historical receipts/pins
+were byte-identical. The API/timers resumed and the pause journal was removed.
+
+That same populated Drive set restored into an independent Windows off-host
+PostgreSQL 18 cluster and filesystem in a 9 GiB noswap tmpfs, with separate data/
+socket and no TCP listener. All 82 table counts, six referenced blobs, image-table
+and catalog/user-context digests, ownership/normalized grants, lineage/receipt/order
+and owner/runtime SCRAM authentication matched the captured backup inventory.
+Existing user data was preserved without imposing empty Watchlist/Settings rules.
+No Proxmox fallback or VM retrieval credentials were used; no persistent plaintext
+dump was saved on Windows. Temporary cluster/plaintext/configuration/runtime/helper
+copies were removed; production records/images/backups remain retained.
+
+The old independent WSL SQLAlchemy 1.4 runtime could not import the new verifier
+before any cluster or retrieval. A disposable runtime matching production Python
+3.13.15 and exact hash-locked libraries resolved this observed incompatibility.
+The SQLAlchemy verifier uses its normal tuple-row DBAPI connection and explicit
+UTC transaction. No application dependency/release changed or new backup ran.
+Two bounded orchestration corrections finalized the already completed pre-migration
+backup's prefixed CLI receipt and restored paused timers before activation health.
+No migration/deployment was repeated or application data repaired.
+
+The short final check passed all 14 normal health/storage/backup checks with active
+API/Caddy/PostgreSQL and backup/retention/health timers; zero failed units. The source
+review found no blocking defect. [Review package](https://github.com/abrianbaker80/Brickvault_Apprisal_App/tree/astra-response/astra_response/Phase-13/13C/r1)
+contains the exact twenty-file candidate, patch and sanitized evidence.
+Main HEAD stays at the accepted 13B local commit; 13C is uncommitted, index empty,
+protected bytes unchanged and main unpushed. This is ready for independent final
+review; Phase 13 remains IN PROGRESS and Phase 14 NOT STARTED.
+
+Earlier sections are dated history; their unapproved-policy and next-step statements
+are superseded by this authorization.
